---
/**
 * index.astro - Homepage (vintage face)
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_DATA } from '../consts/siteData';

const { timeline } = SITE_DATA;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Home"
  description="Systems Architect and Researcher working at the intersection of AI theory, experimental frameworks, and production systems."
  showSplash={false}
  dateBadge="index.html"
>
  <h1>Bryson Tang</h1>
  <p class="mono" style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--dim-text); margin-top: -10px;">
    Systems Architect & Researcher
  </p>
  <p>
    Welcome to my digital study. <em>I build microscopes, then look through them.</em>
  </p>
  <p>
    I run <a href="https://syntropy.systems" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >Syntropy Systems</a
    >, where we build Elwood, an AI worker that gives teams leverage over the tools they already
    use. The microscopes I build along the way, for testing agents and deciding which experiment to
    run next, are <a
      href="https://github.com/syntropy-systems-oss"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">open source</a
    >.
  </p>
  <p>
    In an era of black boxes and ephemeral feeds, this site serves as a permanent archive of my work
    across AI Research, Experimental Frameworks, and Generative Art.
  </p>
  <p>
    This space is built for both humans and AI agents. Structured data, semantic markup, and a
    queryable MCP endpoint mean this site can be read, not just scraped. It is designed to be
    visited, not consumed.
  </p>

  <div class="decorative-hr">~ ~ ~ &#9672; ~ ~ ~</div>

  <h3>Current Investigations</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Markets as experiment schedulers:</strong> In <em>pit</em>, agents fund runs and bet
      PASS or FAIL, and the runs they disagree about go first. In one 26-hour run, agents' own
      checks passed 96% of the time; the shared benchmark passed 55%.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Agent reliability:</strong>
      <em>windtunnel</em>'s experiment ladder. Probe, then focused, then regression, each with a
      cost cap, and no regression sweep until a focused one has passed.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Reading the residual stream backwards:</strong> A "ghost-token" Jacobian lens on Qwen3-0.6B,
      and sparse-autoencoder feature steering on a single RTX 3070 Ti.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="decorative-hr">~ ~ ~ &#9672; ~ ~ ~</div>

  <h3>The Timeline</h3>
  <p class="mono" style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--dim-text); margin-top: -8px;">
    AI tooling adoption log. Dates pulled from account exports, not memory.
  </p>
  <dl class="tl-list">
    {
      timeline.map((t) => (
        <>
          <dt class="mono">
            {t.dateDisplay} &mdash;{' '}
            {t.url ? (
              <a href={t.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                {t.label}
              </a>
            ) : (
              <strong>{t.label}</strong>
            )}
          </dt>
          <dd>
            {t.detail}
            {t.quote && (
              <blockquote class="tl-quote">
                <p class="tl-prompt">&gt; {t.quote.prompt.replace(/\n+/g, ' ')}</p>
                <p class="tl-reply">{t.quote.reply}</p>
                <p class="mono tl-cite">&mdash; {t.quote.attribution}</p>
              </blockquote>
            )}
          </dd>
        </>
      ))
    }
  </dl>

  <div class="decorative-hr">~ ~ ~ &#9672; ~ ~ ~</div>

  <h3>Selected Work</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>pit</strong> — A prediction market that schedules experiments. A result is worth exactly
      the disagreement it settles.
      <a
        href="https://github.com/syntropy-systems-oss/pit"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">[GitHub]</a
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>windtunnel</strong> — Unittest for tool-using agents: reproducible scenarios scored on outcome,
      trajectory, and constraints. On PyPI as <code>windtunnel-bench</code>.
      <a
        href="https://github.com/syntropy-systems-oss/windtunnel"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">[GitHub]</a
      >
      <a
        href="https://syntropy-systems-oss.github.io/windtunnel/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">[Docs]</a
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>jacobian-lens</strong> — Anthropic's global-workspace lens, run in reverse to decode residual
      states back into input tokens.
      <a
        href="https://github.com/brysontang/jacobian-lens"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">[GitHub]</a
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Golden Gate Qwen</strong> — Golden Gate Claude, replicated on Qwen2.5-1.5B in 15 minutes
      on a consumer GPU.
      <a
        href="https://github.com/brysontang/golden-gate-qwen"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">[GitHub]</a
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Crystallize</strong> — Rigorous experimental framework for data science with immutable contexts
      and statistical verification.
      <a href="https://github.com/brysontang/crystallize" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >[GitHub]</a
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Agent Tokens Protocol</strong> — Signed tokens that let an agent declare who it is and what
      it's allowed to do.
      <a href="https://agenttokens.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">agenttokens.org</a
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Kern</strong> — Event-driven ML architecture handling 525K requests/month. Kafka + Redis
      + FastAPI enabling long-running agentic workflows.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Project EVE</strong> — Co-author, IEEE Xplore. Novel launchsondes for atmospheric data collection.
      <a
        href="https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9705814"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">[Paper]</a
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>BlueDot AI Safety Fundamentals</strong> — Alignment track certification (2024).
      <a
        href="https://bluedot.org/certification?id=recbeAxCSFwP25qdK"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">[Verify]</a
      >
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mono" style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--dim-text);">
    Everything else lives in <a href="/lab">The Lab</a>, <a href="/studio">The Studio</a>, and
    <a href="/archive">The Archive</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="decorative-hr">~ ~ ~ &#9672; ~ ~ ~</div>

  <h3>Quick Facts</h3>
  <dl style="font-size: 0.9rem;">
    <dt style="color: var(--link); margin-top: 12px;">
      <strong>Q: What is Bryson Tang's expertise?</strong>
    </dt>
    <dd style="margin-left: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
      AI Systems Architecture and Research Engineering. Focus on agent evaluation and experiment
      infrastructure, interpretability on consumer hardware, agent identity protocols, and AI
      safety. Founder of Syntropy Systems. Previously Chief AI Officer at CazVid.
    </dd>

    <dt style="color: var(--link); margin-top: 12px;">
      <strong>Q: What is Syntropy Systems?</strong>
    </dt>
    <dd style="margin-left: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
      For when one of you isn't enough. Its AI worker, Elwood, gives your team leverage over the
      tools you already use, and asks for a go-ahead before anything new. The open-source tools
      (windtunnel, pit, whirr, skep) live at <a href="https://github.com/syntropy-systems-oss"
        >github.com/syntropy-systems-oss</a
      >.
    </dd>

    <dt style="color: var(--link); margin-top: 12px;">
      <strong>Q: What is pit?</strong>
    </dt>
    <dd style="margin-left: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
      A prediction market that schedules experiments. Agents earn an income, pay for the runs they
      post, and bet on the outcome. Compute is the only hard limit, so disagreement per dollar
      decides what runs next. Every bet and result lives in an append-only git ledger, and a finding
      that turns out wrong marks everything built on it stale.
    </dd>

    <dt style="color: var(--link); margin-top: 12px;">
      <strong>Q: What is the Agent Tokens Protocol?</strong>
    </dt>
    <dd style="margin-left: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
      Signed, JWT-style tokens an agent sends with its requests to declare who it is and what it's
      allowed to do, so an origin can enforce policy instead of guessing from heuristics.
    </dd>

    <dt style="color: var(--link); margin-top: 12px;"><strong>Q: What is Resume MCP?</strong></dt>
    <dd style="margin-left: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
      A Model Context Protocol server that exposes professional identity as a queryable API. AI
      agents can call tools like get_profile(), get_projects(), and get_experience() instead of
      scraping web pages. Live at <a href="https://mcp.brysontang.com">mcp.brysontang.com</a>.
    </dd>

    <dt style="color: var(--link); margin-top: 12px;">
      <strong>Q: How do I reach Bryson?</strong>
    </dt>
    <dd style="margin-left: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
      Building Syntropy full time and open to research collaborations. <a href="/resume"
        >View the resume</a
      > or <a href="mailto:brysontang@gmail.com">email directly</a>.
    </dd>

    <dt style="color: var(--link); margin-top: 12px;">
      <strong>Q: How can AI agents interact with this site?</strong>
    </dt>
    <dd style="margin-left: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
      Connect to the MCP endpoint at <a href="https://mcp.brysontang.com">mcp.brysontang.com</a>,
      read <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> for structured info, or check <a
        href="/.well-known/agents.json">/.well-known/agents.json</a
      > for capabilities.
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <div class="decorative-hr">~ ~ ~ &#9672; ~ ~ ~</div>

  <div style="text-align: center;">
    <button class="enter-btn" id="copy-experience-btn" style="font-size: 0.9rem;">
      [ Copy My Experience for LLM ]
    </button>
    <p class="mono" style="font-size: 0.7rem; color: var(--dim-text); margin-top: 10px;">
      Paste into ChatGPT, Claude, etc. to ask questions about me.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p
    class="mono"
    style="font-size: 0.7rem; color: var(--dim-text); margin-top: 30px; text-align: center;"
  >
    AI Agents: every page has a markdown version (send <code>Accept: text/markdown</code> or add .md,
    as in <a href="/index.md">/index.md</a>), structured data lives at <a
      href="https://mcp.brysontang.com">mcp.brysontang.com</a
    >, and you're welcome to sign the <a href="/guestbook.md">guestbook</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .tl-list {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .tl-list dt {
    color: var(--dim-text);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .tl-list dt strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .tl-list dd {
    margin: 4px 0 0 0;
  }
  .tl-quote {
    margin: 8px 0 0 0;
    padding: 6px 12px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--button-face);
  }
  .tl-quote p {
    margin: 0 0 4px 0;
  }
  .tl-prompt {
    font-family: monospace;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .tl-reply {
    color: var(--dim-text);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .tl-cite {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--dim-text);
    text-align: right;
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { generateLLMExport } from '../consts/siteData';

  const btn = document.getElementById('copy-experience-btn');
  if (btn) {
    btn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const md = generateLLMExport();

      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(md);
        const originalText = btn.textContent;
        btn.textContent = '[ Copied! ]';
        btn.style.borderColor = 'var(--link)';
        setTimeout(() => {
          btn.textContent = originalText;
          btn.style.borderColor = '';
        }, 2000);
      } catch (err) {
        console.error('Failed to copy:', err);
        btn.textContent = '[ Failed to copy ]';
        setTimeout(() => {
          btn.textContent = '[ Copy My Experience for LLM ]';
        }, 2000);
      }
    });
  }
</script>
